    <string name="auto_books">Auto-add books</string>
    <string name="auto_books_short">Auto-add</string>
    <string name="auto_books_desc">When you open a book in an e-book app, it goes to the top of your reading list. Only book titles, authors, progress, due dates and covers on the shelf and search screens, and the title and progress on the reading screen, are read; book text and other apps are never seen. Turn on Pebble Desk in Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="open_accessibility">Open Accessibility</string>
    <string name="auto_off_title">Auto-add is off</string>
    <string name="auto_stalled_title">Auto-add has stopped</string>
    <string name="auto_stalled_desc">Pebble Desk is on in Accessibility but isn\'t running. Books you open won\'t be added, and reading time won\'t be tied to a book.\n\nTurn Pebble Desk off and on again in Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="auto_off_desc">Books you open in e-book apps won\'t be added, and reading time won\'t know which book it was. Turn on Pebble Desk in Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="dont_show_again">Don\'t show again</string>
    <string name="density_changed_title">Screen looks enlarged</string>
    <string name="density_changed_desc">Pebble Desk\'s screen DPI has been changed to %1$d. Everything looks larger and part of the home screen won\'t fit.\n\nTo fix: set Pebble Desk\'s DPI to %2$d in the device settings.</string>
    <string name="density_changed_desc_boox">Pebble Desk\'s screen DPI has been changed to %1$d. Everything looks larger and part of the home screen won\'t fit.\n\nTo fix: long-press the Pebble Desk icon in the app list, open Optimize, and set DPI to %2$d or turn optimization off.</string>
